---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

export const prerender = false;
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Underwings Cybersecurity Solutions"
  description="How Underwings Cybersecurity Solutions collects, uses, stores and protects your personal data under the UAE PDPL — what we collect through our website and LinkedIn lead forms, who we share it with, how long we keep it, and your rights."
  keywords="privacy policy, data protection, UAE PDPL, data subject rights, cybersecurity privacy, data security, Underwings privacy"
  wfPage="6920627afaad5c7afb54bfad"
>
  <Header currentPage="" />

  <main id="main" class="main">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-wrapper">
          <div class="heading-wrapper">
            <h1 data-w-id="3478cca7-a5bc-4e2c-421c-e1fa3985c50b" style="filter:blur(3px);opacity:0" class="heading">Privacy Policy</h1>
          </div>
          <div class="privacy-content">
            <div id="w-node-ba7cf52b-0e43-4a2a-1cfc-903a04e7eef7-fb54bfad" class="privacy-content-wrapper">
              <div data-w-id="7fd2dcd1-6712-12ef-3477-e3d863943974" style="filter:blur(3px);opacity:0" class="rich-text w-richtext">
                <p><em>Last updated: 24 September 2026. This version replaces the policy dated 27 May 2026.</em></p>

                <h2>The short version</h2>
                <ul role="list">
                  <li>We collect personal data only when you give it to us: through our website forms, a LinkedIn lead form, an email, a call or a signed engagement.</li>
                  <li>We use it to answer you, send a quote, deliver the service you asked for, and, only if you opt in, send you security updates.</li>
                  <li>We never sell personal data and we never share it with advertisers.</li>
                  <li>We keep enquiry data for 24 months from our last contact, then delete or anonymise it.</li>
                  <li>You can ask to see, correct, delete or export your data at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:contact@underwings.org">contact@underwings.org</a>.</li>
                  <li>We process personal data under the UAE Personal Data Protection Law, Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 (the PDPL). We advise clients on this law, so we hold ourselves to it.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>Who we are</h2>
                <p>Underwings Cybersecurity Solutions ("Underwings", "we", "us") is a cybersecurity consultancy based in the United Arab Emirates. We provide penetration testing and vulnerability assessment (VAPT), ISO 27001, ADHICS v2 and UAE PDPL compliance services, cloud and network security reviews, and security awareness training. For the purposes of the PDPL we are the <strong>controller</strong> of the personal data described in this policy. Our website is <a href="https://underwings.org">underwings.org</a>.</p>

                <h2>What personal data we collect</h2>
                <h3>Information you give us</h3>
                <ul role="list">
                  <li><strong>Contact and enquiry forms on our website:</strong> your name, work email address, company name, phone number (optional), the service you are interested in, and the message you write.</li>
                  <li><strong>LinkedIn Lead Gen Forms:</strong> when you submit one of our lead forms on LinkedIn, LinkedIn passes us the fields on that form, typically your name, work email address, company name and job title, and the name of the campaign you responded to.</li>
                  <li><strong>Newsletter sign-ups and free resource downloads:</strong> your email address and which resource you requested (for example our Security Assessment Checklist).</li>
                  <li><strong>Service waitlists:</strong> your email address, the service you want to hear about, and optionally your name and company.</li>
                  <li><strong>Meeting bookings:</strong> your name, email address, company and the topic you want to discuss, plus the time you chose.</li>
                  <li><strong>Website chat assistant:</strong> the questions you type. Please do not enter passwords, personal identifiers or confidential system details in the chat.</li>
                  <li><strong>Email, phone and meetings:</strong> whatever you choose to tell us, and our notes of the conversation.</li>
                  <li><strong>Client engagements:</strong> contact details of your staff involved in the project, billing details, and, with your written authorisation, technical information about your systems such as configurations, scan results and findings. Job applicants: see the note under "Careers" below.</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
                <ul role="list">
                  <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address, browser and device type, pages visited, and the page you came from. This is collected by our web server and, only if you accept analytics cookies, by Google Analytics.</li>
                  <li><strong>Campaign attribution:</strong> when you arrive from a link carrying campaign tags (for example a LinkedIn ad), we store the campaign source, medium and landing page in a first-party cookie for 90 days so we know which campaign a later enquiry came from. The cookie contains no name, email or other personal identifier.</li>
                  <li><strong>Security signals:</strong> Cloudflare protects our forms against bots and abuse and may process your IP address and browser signals to do so.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>We do not knowingly collect data from anyone under 18, and our services are offered to businesses, not consumers.</p>

                <h2>Why we use it, and on what legal basis</h2>
                <table class="pp-table">
                  <thead><tr><th>Purpose</th><th>Data</th><th>PDPL legal basis</th></tr></thead>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Answering your enquiry, sending a proposal or quote, scheduling a call</td><td data-label="Data">Enquiry, LinkedIn lead form, booking and conversation data</td><td data-label="PDPL legal basis">Our legitimate interest in responding to a business enquiry you made, and steps taken at your request before a contract</td></tr>
                    <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Delivering the services you engage us for and managing the account</td><td data-label="Data">Client engagement, contact and billing data</td><td data-label="PDPL legal basis">Performance of a contract</td></tr>
                    <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Sending our security newsletter or the free resource you requested</td><td data-label="Data">Email address, resource requested</td><td data-label="PDPL legal basis">Your consent, which you can withdraw at any time with the unsubscribe link or by emailing us</td></tr>
                    <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Keeping a record of leads and conversations in our customer relationship management system</td><td data-label="Data">Enquiry and lead data, notes</td><td data-label="PDPL legal basis">Legitimate interest in managing business relationships</td></tr>
                    <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Understanding which pages and campaigns work, and improving the website</td><td data-label="Data">Analytics and attribution data</td><td data-label="PDPL legal basis">Consent for analytics cookies; legitimate interest for aggregate, first-party campaign attribution</td></tr>
                    <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Protecting the website and our systems from abuse</td><td data-label="Data">Technical and security data</td><td data-label="PDPL legal basis">Legitimate interest in security</td></tr>
                    <tr><td data-label="Purpose">Accounting, tax and legal obligations</td><td data-label="Data">Contract and billing records</td><td data-label="PDPL legal basis">Legal obligation</td></tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
                <p>We do not use your personal data for automated decisions that have legal or similarly significant effects on you, and we do not profile you.</p>

                <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
                <p><strong>We do not sell personal data, and we do not share it with advertisers or data brokers.</strong> We share it only with service providers who process it on our instructions under a data-processing agreement, and only as much as each one needs:</p>
                <ul role="list">
                  <li><strong>Zoho Corporation</strong> (USA data centre) — our customer relationship management system, where enquiries, LinkedIn leads and meeting bookings are recorded, and our business email.</li>
                  <li><strong>LinkedIn Corporation</strong> (USA/Ireland) — operates the Lead Gen Forms and delivers the form data to us. LinkedIn's own handling of your data is governed by the <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/legal/privacy-policy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">LinkedIn Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
                  <li><strong>Google LLC</strong> (USA) — Google Analytics 4, loaded only after you accept analytics cookies, with IP anonymisation.</li>
                  <li><strong>Cloudflare, Inc.</strong> (USA/global) — DNS, content delivery, and bot protection (Turnstile) on our forms.</li>
                  <li><strong>Brevo</strong> (Sendinblue SAS, France) — delivery of the confirmation and notification emails our website sends.</li>
                  <li><strong>Anthropic PBC</strong> (USA) — powers our website chat assistant. The questions you type are sent to Anthropic to generate a reply, are not used to train its models, and are not stored by us.</li>
                  <li><strong>DigitalOcean, LLC</strong> — hosts the server that runs our website and its database (see "Where your data is stored").</li>
                  <li><strong>Meeting scheduling provider</strong> — currently Calendly, LLC (USA); we are moving scheduling into Zoho.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>We may also disclose personal data when the law requires it, to our professional advisers under confidentiality, or as part of a business transfer, in which case this policy continues to apply.</p>

                <h2>Where your data is stored and cross-border transfers</h2>
                <p>Our website and its database run on a server we control in a DigitalOcean data centre in <strong>Bangalore, India</strong>. Our CRM (Zoho) is hosted in the United States, and the other providers above operate from the United States or the European Union. This means personal data you give us is transferred outside the UAE.</p>
                <p>The PDPL allows transfers to countries with adequate protection, or otherwise with appropriate safeguards. Where a destination is not covered by an adequacy decision of the UAE Data Office, we rely on contractual safeguards with each provider (data-processing agreements and standard contractual terms), transfer only the minimum data the service needs, and where the law requires it, your explicit consent. You can ask us for a summary of these safeguards.</p>

                <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
                <ul role="list">
                  <li><strong>Enquiries, LinkedIn leads and CRM records:</strong> 24 months from our last contact with you, then deleted or anonymised, unless you become a client.</li>
                  <li><strong>Newsletter and resource downloads:</strong> until you unsubscribe or ask us to delete you; suppression records are kept so we do not email you again.</li>
                  <li><strong>Waitlists:</strong> until the service launches and you have been notified, then 12 months.</li>
                  <li><strong>Client engagement records and findings:</strong> for the duration of the engagement plus 7 years, to meet audit, legal and contractual obligations; technical findings are shared only with the stakeholders you authorise.</li>
                  <li><strong>Chat assistant:</strong> we do not store transcripts.</li>
                  <li><strong>Analytics data:</strong> Google Analytics event data is retained for 14 months; our first-party attribution cookie expires after 90 days.</li>
                  <li><strong>Server and security logs:</strong> kept for security monitoring and routinely purged; they are not used to identify you except when investigating an attack.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>Your rights under the PDPL</h2>
                <p>You have the right to:</p>
                <ul role="list">
                  <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal data we hold about you and receive a copy;</li>
                  <li><strong>Correct</strong> data that is inaccurate or incomplete;</li>
                  <li><strong>Delete</strong> your data, subject to legal retention requirements;</li>
                  <li><strong>Restrict or object</strong> to processing, including objecting to direct marketing at any time;</li>
                  <li><strong>Data portability</strong>: receive your data in a structured, commonly used, machine-readable format;</li>
                  <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time where processing is based on consent, without affecting processing done before withdrawal;</li>
                  <li><strong>Complain</strong> to the UAE Data Office if you believe we have not handled your data lawfully.</li>
                </ul>
                <p>To exercise any right, email <a href="mailto:contact@underwings.org">contact@underwings.org</a> with the subject line "Privacy request". We will confirm your identity, respond within 14 days, and there is no charge for a reasonable request.</p>

                <h2>Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
                <p>We keep cookies to a minimum. When you first visit, a banner asks whether you accept analytics cookies; nothing non-essential is set until you do. You can change your choice at any time by clearing your browser's site data for underwings.org.</p>
                <table class="pp-table">
                  <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Type</th><th>Lifetime</th></tr></thead>
                  <tbody>
                    <tr><td data-label="Name"><code>uw-cookie-consent</code></td><td data-label="Purpose">Remembers your cookie choice (stored in your browser's local storage)</td><td data-label="Type">Essential</td><td data-label="Lifetime">Until cleared</td></tr>
                    <tr><td data-label="Name"><code>uw_attr</code></td><td data-label="Purpose">Records the campaign source, medium and landing page of your first visit so a later enquiry can be attributed to it; contains no personal identifier</td><td data-label="Type">First-party, functional</td><td data-label="Lifetime">90 days</td></tr>
                    <tr><td data-label="Name"><code>_ga</code>, <code>_ga_*</code></td><td data-label="Purpose">Google Analytics 4: distinguishes visitors and sessions to measure how the site is used</td><td data-label="Type">Analytics, only with your consent</td><td data-label="Lifetime">Up to 2 years</td></tr>
                    <tr><td data-label="Name"><code>__cf_bm</code>, <code>cf_clearance</code></td><td data-label="Purpose">Cloudflare bot protection and Turnstile challenge on forms</td><td data-label="Type">Essential, security</td><td data-label="Lifetime">Up to 30 minutes / 1 year</td></tr>
                  </tbody>
                </table>
                <p>We do not use advertising cookies or social-media tracking pixels on this website.</p>

                <h2>How we protect your data</h2>
                <p>As a cybersecurity company we apply to ourselves the controls we recommend to clients:</p>
                <ul role="list">
                  <li>All data is encrypted in transit (TLS 1.2 or higher) and at rest.</li>
                  <li>Access to systems holding personal data is restricted to named staff who need it, protected by multi-factor authentication, and reviewed regularly.</li>
                  <li>Our website enforces a strict content security policy, bot protection on every form, and rate limiting.</li>
                  <li>Client findings and technical data are stored in access-controlled repositories and shared only with the stakeholders you authorise.</li>
                  <li>We maintain ISO 27001-aligned security controls, an internal Record of Processing Activities, encrypted daily backups, and we test our own systems.</li>
                  <li>If a personal-data breach is likely to affect your rights, we will notify the UAE Data Office and, where required, you, within the timelines set by the PDPL and its Executive Regulations.</li>
                </ul>

                <h2>Careers</h2>
                <p>If you apply for a role, we process your CV and application details to assess your application, under our legitimate interest in recruitment. Unsuccessful applications are deleted after 12 months unless you ask us to keep your details on file. Send applications and questions to <a href="mailto:careers@underwings.org">careers@underwings.org</a>.</p>

                <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
                <p>We will post any changes on this page with a new "Last updated" date. For material changes we will notify active clients and newsletter subscribers directly.</p>

                <h2>Contact us</h2>
                <p>Privacy questions and data-subject requests: <a href="mailto:contact@underwings.org">contact@underwings.org</a> (subject line "Privacy request")<br>Phone: +971 54 707 8203<br>Underwings Cybersecurity Solutions, United Arab Emirates</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
<style>
